      "writtenOn": "2020-09-24T13:45:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not difficult to add, but I thought that implementation library is what gets installed on device and used at runtime, and in that case `OptionalImplicitSdkLibrary()` should always return the name of the implementation library, because it is added to the manifest, and the manifest is used at runtime. It makes no sense to me to add one library to the manifest (the `OptionalimplicitSdkLibrary()` one), but use another library for dexpreopt (the one returned by the new method). This will cause class loader context mismatch at runtime.",
      "parentUuid": "51981449_9336bad4",
      "revId": "77b528a609032bb4e1363975f82e400bbc7a107d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
