      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T12:38:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, there are several distinct parts to this:\n1. The logical name of the library - this is used in \u003cuses-library\u003e and is currently the same as the name of the java_sdk_library - there are no plans to change this.\n2. The path to the library on the device - something like /system/framework/\u003cname\u003e.jar, where \u003cname\u003e is usually the same as the logical name. There are no plans to change these.\n3. The name of the module that provides the implementation library. Currently the java_sdk_library does that but there are plans to change that to a separate module, probably called `\u003cname\u003e.impl` or something like that.\n\nIt is part 3 that you need to use here.\n\nOn a separate but related issue - which probably affects my work more than yours, if dexpreopt requires the implementation library then we will have a problem optimizing against prebuilts as prebuilts do not currently (and ideally never should) provide the implementation jar.\n\nPresumably, we already have a similar issue with prebuilt apps. Am I right in thinking that in their unbundled build they are unoptimized and they are only optimized while building the system image that contains them?",
      "parentUuid": "643e2b26_583d5c08",
